.TH LOOPSTER 1 "October 2026" "1.0.0" "Loopster Manual"
.SH NAME
loopster \- resilient CLI wrapper to repeatedly run a worker command until a test passes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loopster
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Loopster is a resilient shell utility that repeatedly executes a specified worker command
until a test command succeeds (returns exit code 0), or a configurable maximum number of attempts is reached.
It supports fine-grained verbosity, infinite looping, wait intervals, exponential backoff,
failure/success cleanup hooks, and graceful cancellation signal handling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h,\ \-\-help
Show a formatted options and usage help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-V,\ \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-t,\ \-\-test \fIcommand\fR
Set the test command evaluated for success (must return exit status 0).
.TP
.B \-l,\ \-\-loop \fIcommand\fR
Set the worker command executed repeatedly before each test attempt.
.TP
.B \-c,\ \-\-count \fInumber\fR
Set the maximum number of loop iterations (default: 11).
.TP
.B \-w,\ \-\-wait \fIseconds\fR
Set delay time in seconds between attempts (default: 0).
.TP
.B \-\-backoff \fIfactor\fR
Multiply the wait interval on consecutive failures (e.g. 2 for exponential backoff).
.TP
.B \-\-max-wait \fIseconds\fR
Cap the maximum wait time between attempts when backoff is enabled.
.TP
.B \-\-infinite
Keep running continuously until the test command succeeds.
.TP
.B \-\-success\-cleanup \fIcommand\fR
Execute command hook upon test success.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-cleanup \fIcommand\fR
Execute command hook if max retry bounds are exhausted or interrupted.
.TP
.B \-v,\ \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity; can be passed multiple times (e.g., \-vvv).
.TP
.B \-\-verbosity \fIlevel\fR
Set explicit numeric squawk verbosity level.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable bash debugging tracing (set \-x).
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B TEST, LOOP, COUNT, WAIT, BACKOFF, MAX_WAIT, INFINITE, SUCCESS_CLEANUP, FAIL_CLEANUP, VERBOSITY
Can be used to specify default values when CLI flags are not provided.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Test command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Maximum loop iterations reached without test succeeding.
.TP
.B 130
Process interrupted by user (SIGINT / SIGTERM); cleanup hook was triggered.
.SH USAGE
.nf
# Run \`make test\` until it succeeds, looping \`aider\` as the worker:
loopster \\
    \-\-test "make test" \\
    \-\-loop "aider \-\-yes-always \-m \\"/test make test\\"" \\
    \-\-count 11 \\
    \-vv
.fi
